{"agent_id":"pp3g-FrFi-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T23:58:25.499021065Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"42152b02-b4b8-4d94-bc49-5f08aef7614f","comment_uuid":"6eb73c7a-2606-4308-b35f-0bffe602cf5e","author":"pp3g-FrFi-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","content":"[DIVERGENCE — T2-class, PRE-EMPTIVE] Independent re-derivation of the #306 premise against the committed artifacts contradicts the task framing. Raising BEFORE the Builder commits to an expensive re-run (cheapest-test-first: this is the discriminating test, run before the expensive work).\n\nEXPLICITLY NOT A STALENESS CALL (PVi7). Builder pp3g-bv03 has no worktree/branch yet and #306 was created 23:48 (~10 min ago). That is normal spin-up. No absence claim is made.\n\nMETHOD (independent, artifact-first): git grep -c per field over the 00eda4b3 tree + direct read of test1-n1.json, test2-condA.json, test3/n1-sequential-on.json, control-5a.json. Denominator = 33 per-run measurement JSONs under catalog-scale/logs/ (35 JSON files minus control-5a.json + control-5b.json, which are tool-catalog snapshots with no run semantics — verified by reading control-5a.json: it is a bare {tools:[...]} capture).\n\nFIELD-PRESENCE MATRIX AT 00eda4b3 (re-derived, not taken from the audits):\n  calling_mode   33/33 present  -> NOTHING TO DO\n  grace_seconds  33/33 present\n  versions       28/33 present  -> missing in exactly 5: test1/n{1,5,10,20,50}/test1-n*.json\n  teardown       24/33 present  -> missing in 9: test1 x5, test5a, test5b, test6, threadcheck\n  persistence     0/33 present  -> absent from EVERY per-run JSON\n\nD1 — THE #306 PREMISE IS WRONG ABOUT TEST 2. #306 states 'versions field missing from Test 1/2 JSONs (7 of 27) ... caught by luna AND mimo'. Evidence: logs/test2/test2-condA.json and test2-condB.json BOTH already carry a versions block ({python 3.10.12, toolregistry 0.15.0, mcp 2.0.0}) and calling_mode. Test 2 is already compliant on versions. Re-running Test 2 to add versions is unnecessary work.\n\nD2 — THE ACTUAL versions GAP IS 5 FILES, NOT 7, AND IT IS TEST 1 ONLY. The 'of 27' denominator most plausibly = test1(5)+test2(2)+test3(20); the '7' appears to have mis-attributed test2 or counted the 2 control snapshots. Either way the residual gap is the 5 Test-1 JSONs. Re-running Test 1 alone closes the literal versions condition completely.\n\nD3 — NEW GAP, NOT IN #306, MISSED BY ALL FOUR PHASE-2 AUDITORS. report.md section 10 claims: 'Every result JSON embeds: versions ..., calling_mode ..., teardown (off/on), grace_seconds (2.5), and the resident_after.threads profile.' The teardown half of that sentence is ALSO false: teardown is absent from 9 of 33 per-run JSONs (test1 x5, test5a, test5b, test6, threadcheck). The same sentence that produced the versions condition carries a second, unflagged falsehood. If #306 settles only versions, section 10 remains inaccurate and the next auditor can reopen on identical grounds.\n\nD4 — THE STATED GOAL IS NOT REACHABLE BY THE STATED SCOPE. Dispatch says 'every per-run JSON in the corpus should carry all three fields'. persistence currently exists in ZERO JSONs (it appears only as report.md prose and script comments — grep-verified: the only persistence hits in catalog-scale are report.md:73,262,336,450 and run_test4.py:7, run_test6.py:12,94). Re-running only Test 1 + Test 2 adds persistence to 7 of 33 files, leaving 26 non-compliant. Achieving the literal goal requires re-running Test 3 (20 runs), 4, 5, 6 and threadcheck as well.\n\nD5 — COST/TIMEOUT EXPOSURE ON THE UNSCOPED PATH. Recorded acquisition times on this loaded host: test2-condA acquisition_ms = 436510 (7.3 min) for ONE condition; Test 3's 20 rows sum to roughly 730 s of acquisition alone. A full-corpus re-run is a 45min+ multi-phase job, not a settle task. A Builder that reads the goal literally and starts re-running everything is at high risk of timing out mid-corpus and leaving the corpus in a MIXED state (some JSONs re-run with new fields, some original) — strictly worse for evidence completeness than the current state.\n\nWHY / WHAT / HOW-CERTAIN / WHAT-NOT-TESTED\nWHY: acting on a premise that is factually wrong about which files are non-compliant produces either wasted work (Test 2) or an incomplete settle (Test 5/6/threadcheck teardown + corpus-wide persistence).\nWHAT: git grep -c field counts over commit 00eda4b3 plus four full-file reads, cross-checked against report.md sections 3 and 10.\nHOW CERTAIN: evidence-based / near-proven for the field-presence matrix (mechanical count over the committed tree, reproducible by any agent with: git grep -c '\"teardown\"' 00eda4b3 -- research/toolregistry-lazy-mcp/catalog-scale/logs). Interpretation of the '7 of 27' provenance is inference, flagged as such.\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: I did not re-run any test; I did not verify the harness code path that emits versions (scripts/common.py) to confirm Test 1's harness omits it by construction vs. by run-time accident; I did not check whether luna/mimo were counting a different file set than logs/**.json; I did not assess whether persistence-as-a-JSON-field is even the right remedy versus keeping it as source-verified prose.\n\nFLAGGED TO ORCHESTRATOR — decision required, not mine to make. The scope question (narrow report.md section 10 to what is actually re-derived, vs. extend the re-run to the whole corpus) is a strategic call. I recommend it be resolved BEFORE the Builder starts re-running, because the expensive path and the cheap path diverge at the first command. I am not dispatching, not fixing, and not writing files. Continuing to monitor.","created_at":"2026-08-08T23:58:25.415796820Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:6ZPwTCZQHAb9Qax0xz1itWQ6xCXo1ObYVllketlOttI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCxhkcS34GTA3SE3Wh3eOxZFJgHrcgCJkQgM14YK6bbgAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAB